 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** The coarse-to-fine approach reduces training time compared to optimizing a high-resolution grid from scratch, as the initial coarse grid converges faster. However, the iterative refinement and pruning steps add overhead. The fine detail reconstruction stage adds additional computational cost due to the hybrid explicit-implicit representation and progressive scaling [S2].
-- **Memory Complexity:** Pruning reduces memory usage by removing unoccupied voxels. The fine stage uses a higher-resolution grid but only in the unknown space, balancing memory and detail [S2].
